+## Background
+The method was introduced in the context of point-based rendering, specifically to address the visual discontinuities that appear when a surface is rendered via both splats and polygons without special treatment [S1]. It was developed as part of a broader effort to create efficient hybrid rendering systems for point-based models on GPUs [S1]. The approach leverages the properties of splat weight falloff to achieve smooth transitions without the complexity of additional geometry rasterization [S1].
 
-    ### Multiresolution Hybrid Rendering with Octree
-    A hybrid multi-resolution rendering system based on an octree that switches between splat and polygon representations based on sampling density [S1].
-    *   **What it is:** An extension of the blending method to hierarchical data structures [S1]. Nodes store splat indices; leaves store polygon indices [S1].
-    *   **What sets it apart:** It explicitly manages transition splats across different levels of detail [S1]. Edges shared by polygons in different leaves are explicitly sampled, and splats too close to these edges are removed to avoid oversampling [S1].
-    *   **When to choose it:** When rendering large datasets with varying density where some regions are better represented by polygons (under-sampled) and others by splats [S1].
